cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenPhoneUse in research or a product, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenPhoneUse: an open-source phone-use AI agent that runs on the Android phone itself"
abstract: >-
  OpenPhoneUse is an open-source Android app in which a large language model operates the phone like a
  person: it reads the screen through Android's AccessibilityService and taps, types, scrolls and moves
  between apps, seeing each screen both as an element list and as a numbered screenshot. It runs
  entirely on the phone, without a PC, ADB or root, works with ChatGPT plans, OpenAI, Claude, Grok and
  Gemini models, always asks before paying or changing security settings, asks before deleting unless
  the user asked for that one recoverable item and before sending unless the user named the recipient
  and the text, and never types passwords, handing that step to the user.
type: software
